\pard\li720\sl240\slmult1\b0 Hello, \par
\par
from my benchmark,  to serialize a simple string, rapidjson.dumps take 10x more time than a copy, juste for adding  doubles quotes at both ends  and sometimes escape " ,\\  ,controls characters (ord(c) < 32 including \\b,\\t,\\n,\\f,\\r) and non-ascii characters when ensure_ascii is True and string.isascii() is False .\par
\par
Do you have a idea why ? Does rapidjson go through utf_8 encoding in bytes and utf_8 decoding , that could explain this bad performances compared to copy time ?\par
\par
Otherwise ,  if that is the escape step that take so much time, would it be possible to precise to rapidjson that a string doesn't contain any character needing escape (for example if generated from base64 encoding) with a RawString object for example, or to add internaly a step to check if a string will need escape in order to bypass the rapidjson normal path for strings juste needing  double quotes to the both ends ? \par
\par
I coded an example with a need_escape function that checks if a string needs escaping, although the function is not optimized at all, it already saves a 90% of time on lot of strings.\par
\fs16\par
    import rapidjson\par
    escaped_chars =  set('\\b\\t\\n\\f\\r"\\\\') #& set((chr(i) for i in range(32)))\par
    \par
    #@profile\par
    def need_escape(str_,ensure_ascii):         # 0.45 msec \par
        if ensure_ascii and not str_.isascii():\par
            return True\par
        for c in escaped_chars:\par
            if c in str_:\par
                return True\par
        return False\par
    \par
    #@profile\par
    def dumps_str(str_,ensure_ascii):    # 4.5 msec\par
        return rapidjson.dumps(str_, ensure_ascii=ensure_ascii)  # 4.5 msec if ensure_ascii is False\par
    \par
    #@profile\par
    def dumps_str_optimized(str_,ensure_ascii,need_escape): # 0.75 msec\par
        if not need_escape :\par
            return (f'"\{str_\}"')    # 0.26 msec\par
        return rapidjson.dumps(str_, ensure_ascii=ensure_ascii)  # 4.5 msec if ensure_ascii is False\par
    \par
    str_long = "A"* 1200000\par
    for i in [8,9,10,12,13] + list(range(32,132)):\par
        char = chr(i)\par
        str_  =   str_long + char # worse case\par
        for ensure_ascii in [True,False]:\par
            encoded = dumps_str(str_,ensure_ascii)\par
            encoded_optimized = dumps_str_optimized(str_,ensure_ascii,need_escape = need_escape(str_,ensure_ascii))\par
       )\par
